{
  "info": {
    "name": "FoC Credit Service",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "AI Assistance Disclosure: Tool: Claude Code (model: Claude Opus 5.5), date: 2026-10-11. Scope: generated this collection from the routes and error codes in credit-service/AGENTS.md. Author review: pending — Jian Bing to record what he checked. 2026-10-14 (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5): added the Balance folder. 2026-10-15 (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5): added the Dead letters folder. 2026-10-18 (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5): added the transaction history requests to the Balance folder (route decided by Jian Bing). 2026-10-18 (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5): folders 1–3 create their users' wallets through UserRegistered, and a reserve with no wallet answers 409 (#79; decided by Jian Bing).\n\nRequests for the Credit Service's internal routes, which only the Order Service calls. They go straight to the service on port 3004, not through the gateway.\n\nSETUP: set the serviceKey collection variable to CREDIT_SERVICE_KEY from your .env, and start the service and Kafka UI with `docker compose up -d credit-service kafka-ui`. Wallets come only from UserRegistered (#79), so folders 1–3 first publish one for each new user through Kafka UI (kafkaUiUrl, local only).\n\nRUN each folder top to bottom (or with the Collection Runner). The first request of each folder makes fresh ids, so folders can be re-run any number of times. A new user starts with 10 credits."
  },
